11. {−3, −4}
To give −37,129 a value between −100 and −1, you must shift the decimal point to change the number to −37.129 or −3.7129. This requires a shift of either three or four places to the left. Multiplication by a positive exponent shifts the decimal point to the right. To shift the decimal point three places to the left, multiply by 10−3. To shift it four places to the left, multiply by
10−4. Therefore, the exponent j = {−3, −4}.
